        "date":  "2026-10-13",
        "theme":  "Support",
        "summary":  "ShipStation Global built Deckhand, an AI IT help desk agent for Slack using Amazon Bedrock AgentCore and Anthropic\u0027s Claude, that resolved 97.5% of incoming queries in its first three months with a 96% positive employee feedback rating. The system deflected approximately 812 support conversations, saving an estimated 1,600 hours annually, and handles 30-100 messages daily including 94% of after-hours inquiries. The knowledge base indexes Confluence articles, intranet pages, PDFs, and mined Slack threads.",
        "execSummary":  "A 97.5% resolution rate on IT support queries with 96% positive feedback is an exceptionally strong outcome for an AI support deployment, and the after-hours coverage addresses one of the most persistent gaps in enterprise IT support models. For customer-support and IT leaders, this case study is notable because the architecture, Slack-native, Jira-integrated, knowledge base drawn from existing internal documentation, is replicable without significant custom engineering. The key design decision to mine resolved Slack threads as training data is a practical technique that converts institutional knowledge into agent capability. The caveat: the 97.5% resolution rate likely reflects a relatively well-scoped IT knowledge domain; the same approach applied to broader customer-facing support will require more rigorous escalation design and quality monitoring.",
