        "summary":  "NVIDIA\u0027s Nemotron 3 Ultra model, optimized with LangChain\u0027s Deep Agents harness, achieved the highest accuracy among open models on the LangChain Deep Agents benchmark, reaching performance parity with top closed models at approximately one-tenth the inference cost. Improvements came entirely from harness engineering, system prompts, tool descriptions, and middleware, without any model retraining. Early adopters include Abridge, Amdocs, Box, and EY.",
        "execSummary":  "The central finding here, benchmark-leading agentic performance achieved through harness engineering rather than model retraining, has direct implications for enterprise AI economics: the configuration layer around a model may matter as much as the model itself, which means enterprises have meaningful optimization leverage without incurring fine-tuning costs. At one-tenth the inference cost of comparable closed models, Nemotron 3 Ultra combined with LangChain becomes a serious contender for high-throughput agent workloads where closed-model pricing is prohibitive. For leaders evaluating open versus closed model strategies, this result reinforces the case for open-weight models in cost-sensitive, high-volume enterprise deployments, particularly where data sovereignty or customization requirements make closed APIs unsuitable. The caveat is that harness engineering requires specialized expertise that many enterprise teams do not currently have in-house.",
