        "execSummary":  "Connecting AI agents is the solved problem; making them think coherently together is the unsolved one. Enterprises scaling multi-agent workflows will hit a wall where agents technically communicate but still produce incoherent or conflicting outputs. The Internet of Cognition framework gives CIOs a concrete vocabulary for what their agent infrastructure must support beyond API connectivity. The key caveat: this architecture is still emerging, so enterprises building now should design for retrofitting these coordination layers rather than assuming current agent platforms will handle it natively.",
