        "summary":  "A Workato survey of IT leaders found nearly two-thirds anticipate AI agents will generate public security incidents within the next 18 months, with roughly one-third indicating they would attempt to handle such incidents discreetly. Most enterprise AI agents currently lack formal IT department approval, highlighting widespread shadow AI adoption. The findings reveal critical governance gaps around monitoring, control, and accountability for autonomous AI systems.",
        "execSummary":  "The combination of high incident expectation and a one-third intent to conceal those incidents is a board-level governance red flag, not just an IT operations issue. Enterprises deploying AI agents without formal IT approval are building liability exposure at scale, and the shadow AI dynamic means security teams may not even know their attack surface. For customer-support and operations leaders, the immediate action is an AI agent inventory audit, mapping every autonomous workflow to a named human owner and formal approval status. The broader implication: the speed of agentic AI adoption has outpaced the governance infrastructure needed to manage it safely.",
